"""
MORPHEUS blink / yawn test: PRE-EVA vs POST-EVA   (JSON output, ONEIROS cv.raw)

Tracks blinks, eye closure and yawns from the camera (MediaPipe Face Mesh) during
two 30-second trials and saves each trial as JSON. No Excel, no charts.

Workflow
  1. PRE-EVA starts automatically; its 30 s window opens at the first frame with a face.
  2. When it finishes, press  P  to start POST-EVA (P is ignored until PRE-EVA is done).
  3. Each trial is saved as JSON. With --person it is also built into an ONEIROS
     cv.raw message (test "blink"), validated against the contract schema and,
     with --mqtt-host, published.

Windows (event time, tumbling, non-overlapping)
  A trial is ONE 30 s window [t0, t0 + 30). t0 is the capture time of the first
  frame with a face. A frame belongs to a window by the time it was CAPTURED, not
  when it was processed. Start inclusive, end exclusive: nothing is in two windows,
  and POST-EVA only starts after PRE-EVA's window has closed.
  A blink or yawn belongs to the window in which it BEGAN. If one is still in
  progress when the window ends, the window stays open (at most GRACE_MAX_S) only
  to let that episode finish; frames after t0 + 30 add nothing else.

Files (in --outdir, default ./eva_data)
  blink_pre_eva_<timestamp>.json, blink_post_eva_<timestamp>.json, eva_blink_schema.json
  With --person: blink_pre_eva_<timestamp>.cv_raw.json / blink_post_eva_...cv_raw.json

Install:  pip install opencv-python numpy "mediapipe==0.10.21" jsonschema paho-mqtt
Run:      python Drowsiness_json.py
          python Drowsiness_json.py --person PSEUDO-001 --session s-2026-11-13-01 --mqtt-host BROKER_IP
          python Drowsiness_json.py --camera recording.mp4 --person PSEUDO-001   (replay a video)
Keys:     P = start POST-EVA,  m = face mesh on/off,  q / ESC = quit

This is a demo tool, not a medical device.
"""

